maps.summary:
Profile persistence lives in mountain/server/Profiles.luau (validation, load and migration hook, lease lock, save, durable transact) and mountain/server/Store.luau (the DataStore adapter plus a JSON round-trip memory mock). The pure defaults and migration live in mountain/shared/Rules.luau (newProfile) and mountain/shared/RunRules.luau (Run.migrate, schema 1 to 2). The current schema is 2. Load accepts only schema 1 or 2. An unknown schema is refused and left untouched. The house pattern for additive data has no version bump: an optional field is nil-tolerated in valid() and filled on load (settings, bats, tycoon). valid() is a whitelist of required keys and never rejects unknown keys. It runs on the saved profile BEFORE migration and again before every save and transaction. So a new field that is made required, or that the code can push out of range, either locks every existing player out or freezes their saves.

To add player XP/level, purchase receipts, owned skins and a creature origin tag safely, each item needs these steps:
(1) default in R.newProfile;
(2) an optional `x==nil or valid(x)` check in Profiles.valid;
(3) a fill/normalize step inside the load transform after Custody.migrate, so it persists on first save;
(4) bounded, JSON-safe shapes: string-keyed sets or dense capped arrays, like securedRunIds (cap 128);
(5) mutations through P.transact, with a profile-stored idempotency ledger that mutate checks first;
(6) tests in run_persistence.luau and run_ui_server.py (legacy profile without the field loads and persists; malformed field fails closed with no overwrite; replay grants once), plus StudioTests for real HttpService JSON.

Purchases also need a new UIProtocol action and a UIRequests branch. Today no request id reaches the dispatcher, so the id has to be passed through, or a nonce carried in the payload. The egg roll currently lives in a local function in Main and must move to shared so the odds shown are the odds used. The skin cannot be stored under p.bats, because BatRules.normalize rebuilds that table and drops unknown keys. The origin tag must survive hatching: R.hatch copies only the species today. It must also be enforced in R.equip, in the valid() team check and in Competition.snapshot. Server files are not in sync_hud.py's manifest, so P2 server edits will not reach Studio until that is extended. Baseline (run read-only now): run_persistence 28, run_ui_server 25, run_lifecycle 8, run_rules 23, rules 121, ui_protocol 42, all PASS.

facts.claim:
Anti-abuse on all world prompts:
- per-player 0.35 s limiter and busy check;
- interact requires safe(player) (not inside the post-teleport block window) and being within 15 studs;
- R.canEnter is always true for sections 1-6, so there is no gating.
